tatement_1t4cy_249","children":"For a uniform label reassignment independent of the data, the normalized maximum scan exceeds a constant multiple of its tail inflation factor with joint probability at most 2e^{-t}, even under the bounded Gaussian alternative."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"_prerequisites_1t4cy_251","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Uses."}]," ",[["$","span","assumption-6-1",{"children":[false,["$","a",null,{"href":"#assumption-6-1","children":"Assumption 6.1"}]]}],["$","span","assumption-6-2",{"children":[" · ",["$","a",null,{"href":"#assumption-6-2","children":"Assumption 6.2"}]]}],["$","span","Uniform random assignment independent of data",{"children":[" · ","Uniform random assignment independent of data"]}],["$","span","definition-4-5",{"children":[" · ",["$","a",null,{"href":"#definition-4-5","children":"Definition 4.5"}]]}],["$","span","lemma-b-2",{"children":[" · ",["$","a",null,{"href":"#lemma-b-2","children":"Lemma B.2"}]]}],["$","span","lemma-b-3",{"children":[" · ",["$","a",null,{"href":"#lemma-b-3","children":"Lemma B.3"}]]}]]]}],[["$","figure","eq-6-10",{"className":"_equation_1t4cy_259","id":"eq-6-10","aria-label":"the joint probability that the randomized scan exceeds C two kappa t is at most two e to minus t","children":[["$","div",null,{"dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$a6"}}],"$La7"]}]],"$La8","$La9"]}]
4e:["$","article","remark-6-5",{"className":"_proofCard_1t4cy_227","id":"remark-6-5","data-kind":"remark","children":[["$","header",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"#remark-6-5","children":["Remark 6.5","."]}]," ","The new proof ingredient"]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"remark"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"_statement_1t4cy_249","children":"The nonstandard step is simultaneous control of hypergeometric signal leakage and matrix fluctuation after repartitioning two different Gaussian populations, uniformly over overlapping generalized-eigenvalue blocks."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"_prerequisites_1t4cy_251","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Uses."}]," ",[["$","span","lemma-6-4",{"children":[false,["$","a",null,{"href":"#lemma-6-4","children":"Lemma 6.4"}]]}]]]}],[],false,["$","p",null,{"className":"_resolution_1t4cy_275","children":[["$","em",null,{"children":"Interpretation."}]," ","Lemma 6.4 closes the gap between the actual permutation threshold and the analytic minimax scale."," ",["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","em",null,{"children":"Scope."}]," ","Generic permutation-power results do not automatically imply this nonsmooth overlapping-block eigenvalue bound."]}]]}]]}]
50:["$","figcaption",null,{"children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"#eq-6-15","children":"(6.15)-(6.16)"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"_screenReaderOnly_1t4cy_269","children":"a separated population root implies power at least one minus beta"}]]}]
51:["$","p",null,{"className":"_proofText_1t4cy_273","children":[["$","em",null,{"children":"Proof."}]," ","Lemma 6.3 puts the observed score above a fixed threshold with failure beta/2. Use Lemma 6.4 and Fubini to bound the expected non-identity conditional orbit tail. Markov's inequality converts the joint tail into a high-probability conditional tail. Combine the identity mass and residual orbit budget to obtain p <= alpha."," ",["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":"□"}]]}]
52:["$","p",null,{"className":"_resolution_1t4cy_275","children":[["$","em",null,{"children":"Consequently."}]," ","The actual full-permutation test, not a surrogate analytic scan, receives a finite-sample power guarantee."," ",["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","em",null,{"children":"Scope."}]," ","The constants are non-sharp and the theorem remains inside the balanced Gaussian moderate-dimensional regime."]}]]}]
53:["$","article","remark-6-7",{"className":"_proofCard_1t4cy_227","id":"remark-6-7","data-kind":"remark","children":[["$","header",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"#remark-6-7","children":["Remark 6.7","."]}]," ","Orbit resolution"]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"remark"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"_statement_1t4cy_249","children":"The full-permutation p-value cannot be smaller than one over the orbit size, so |G|^{-1} <= alpha is necessary for rejection; in a balanced two-sample orbit this condition becomes automatic quickly as N grows."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"_prerequisites_1t4cy_251","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Uses."}]," ",[["$","span","definition-5-3",{"children":[false,["$","a",null,{"href":"#definition-5-3","children":"Definition 5.3"}]]}],["$","span","theorem-6-6",{"children":[" · ",["$","a",null,{"href":"#theorem-6-6","children":"Theorem 6.6"}]]}]]]}],[],false,["$","p",null,{"className":"_resolution_1t4cy_275","children":[["$","em",null,{"children":"Interpretation."}]," ","The theorem reserves the usable alpha budget after accounting for the identity mass."," ",["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","em",null,{"children":"Scope."}]," ","A tiny orbit can make a formally valid test unable to reject."]}]]}]]}]
54:["$","article","remark-6-8",{"className":"_proofCard_1t4cy_227","id":"remark-6-8","data-kind":"remark","children":[["$","header",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"#remark-6-8","children":["Remark 6.8","."]}]," ","Why the Markov step matters"]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"remark"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"_statement_1t4cy_249","children":"Power depends on a data-conditional permutation tail, whereas Lemma 6.4 is joint in data and permutation; Markov's inequality is the explicit bridge from the joint expectation to the high-probability conditional bound."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"_prerequisites_1t4cy_251","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Uses."}]," ",[["$","span","lemma-6-4",{"children":[false,["$","a",null,{"href":"#lemma-6-4","children":"Lemma 6.4"}]]}],["$","span","theorem-6-6",{"children":[" · ",["$","a",null,{"href":"#theorem-6-6","children":"Theorem 6.6"}]]}]]]}],[],false,["$","p",null,{"className":"_resolution_1t4cy_275","children":[["$","em",null,{"children":"Interpretation."}]," ","An analogy between analytic and permutation thresholds cannot replace this conditioning step."," ",["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","em",null,{"children":"Scope."}]," ","The conversion is conservative and does not yield a sharp conditional quantile approximation."]}]]}]]}]
